      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-284393",
      ":question/problem": "Amir and Jenna bought notebooks and binders at a school supply shop. The cost of each notebook was the same, as was the cost of each binder. Amir bought $5$ notebooks and $3$ binders for $$71$. In contrast, Jenna bought $2$ notebooks and $6$ binders for $$84$.\n\nWhich of the following systems of linear equations represents this situation if $x$ is the price, in dollars, of each notebook and $y$ is the price, in dollars, of each binder?"
    },
